# man-db runtime identity (canonical, fixed): user man UID 65,
# primary group man GID 13 (base-seeded). Upstream builds with
# MAN_OWNER=man (cache files owned by man).
# UID 65 sits in the preferred 0..199 packaged range - never reuse it
# for another identity.
# Ordering note: any historical manual man entry with a different UID
# (e.g. a local 999 bodge) must be removed BEFORE the first install of
# this package - a same-name/different-UID entry is a fatal conflict.
user man 65 man /var/cache/man /sbin/nologin
group man 13
dir /var/cache/man 0755 man man
